WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
ToonStudio is more than a tool for drawing a single image. It is a browser-based creative workspace that connects the stages around webtoon production in one work.

2
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Move from planning into 2D and 3D production, project management, review and publishing preparation without losing the context of the story.

3
00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:18.000
The story workspace helps shape the world, characters, wants, obstacles and working premise before visual production begins.

4
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Keep episode goals, scene intent and dialogue in production context so the next stage knows what needs to be drawn.

5
00:01:48.000 --> 00:02:21.000
The drawing workspace keeps the canvas central while brushes, layers, selection and editing tools stay close to the work.

6
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:54.000
Open texture, filters and color correction when needed while preserving as much screen space as possible for the manuscript itself.

7
00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:21.000
Turn a scene into readable storytelling through panel layout, dialogue, balloons and the rhythm of a vertical scroll.

8
00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:48.000
Instead of separating art and text, refine eye flow and direction inside the same manuscript context.

9
00:03:48.000 --> 00:04:24.000
In the 3D workspace, compose character poses, environments and space to explore difficult shots quickly from multiple angles.

10
00:04:24.000 --> 00:05:00.000
Check cameras and shot transitions, then return that result to the current 2D manuscript as a practical scene-planning reference.

11
00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:27.000
The AI workspace uses creator-controlled runtime and generation tools to assist repetitive production and idea exploration.

12
00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:54.000
Automation does not make the final decision: creators remain responsible for reviewing, selecting and applying results to the work.

13
00:05:54.000 --> 00:06:27.000
Projects keep owners, production state and next actions connected to the actual work instead of separate status documents.

14
00:06:27.000 --> 00:07:00.000
Revision requests, change history and review stay connected, reducing missed handoffs and bottlenecks caused by file-only workflows.

15
00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:24.000
The learning area covers the webtoon production process, drawing and story techniques, practical exercises and references close to the work.

16
00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:48.000
Creative resources such as assets and audio also stay near production, helping creators find a useful next action when a stage stalls.

17
00:07:48.000 --> 00:08:06.000
At the finishing stage, check manuscript images, work information and publishing settings, then validate the required output conditions.

18
00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:24.000
From planning through production, 3D, collaboration, review, export and publishing preparation: start where you need and keep moving inside the same work.
